&paper=expository&passage=density-and-approximation","span":{"end_byte":59209,"end_line":1405,"start_byte":58470,"start_line":1396},"stage":"expository"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=scalar.smooth_positive_density&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=scalar.smooth_positive_density&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=scalar.smooth_positive_density&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=scalar.smooth_positive_density&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&ref=sha256%3A9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5%2Fnodes%2Fscalar.smooth_positive_density","record":{"assumption_ids":["scalar.paper_minimizer"],"boundary":"Additional moment-bootstrap and fixed-time flattening argument. Not part of FullSupportConclusion and not needed by the QAOA scalar construction; do not place it in that prerequisite closure. The numerical lower bound is an ordinary deduction in long §9.2, not an extra clause of the selected formal endpoint; it depends on the same minimizer and moment normalization.","citation_ids":["scalar-r2-26-cite-smooth-positive-density"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_reconstruction_bounds_20261024"],"id":"scalar.smooth_positive_density","kind":"claim","label":"Further manuscript corollary: smooth positive density","locator":"order-parameter-regularity.tex:15–152; cor:smooth-measure","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-order-parameter-regularity","statement":"For an admissible minimizer, gamma(0)=0, gamma∈C∞([0,1)), gamma=E Phi_xxx²/(2 E Phi_xx³), and mu(dt)=gamma′(t)dt. For 0<t<1, 2 gamma′ E Phi_xx³≥gamma(t)² E Phi_xx⁴/1000>0. Only gamma′(0)≥0 is asserted at zero. Since E Phi_xx²=1 and Phi_xx>=0, moment Cauchy–Schwarz gives E Phi_xx³<=sqrt(E Phi_xx⁴)<=E Phi_xx⁴. Hence gamma′(t)>=gamma(t)²/2000 for 0<t<1, and mu((r,s])>=(s-r)gamma(r)²/2000 for 0<r<s<1.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","id":"field:08bd73645852b0b9c0d92aedee4bfec5faa93de84bc2304e50abc8bf97dee6d0","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.paper_minimizer"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22scalar.smooth_positive_density%22%2C%22support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22scalar.smooth_positive_density%22%2C%22support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd4